13. Falsification Conditions

This thesis must be falsifiable.

I will materially reduce my conviction if several of the following occur.

Connectedness fails to become real

Google continues putting Gemini branding on many products, but the underlying state, context and task continuity remain siloed.

Cross-device AI remains superficial

Watch, glasses, car and laptop receive separate Gemini interfaces but do not become meaningfully connected surfaces of one intelligence system.

Personal context fails to create better outcomes

More data access creates noise, privacy friction or weak incremental utility rather than materially better decisions and actions.

Search economics deteriorate

AI features increase usage but reduce monetization enough that Search's economic engine weakens structurally.

Google fails to capture value from agent interoperability

A2A becomes widely adopted but Google Cloud gains little advantage in hosting, discovery, governance, identity, security or execution.

Agent Registry remains peripheral

The product fails to become an important control plane for enterprise agents and is easily substituted without meaningful switching costs.

A third party owns the interface

Another AI platform becomes the primary user-level agent on Android, Chrome or the web while treating Google as replaceable backend infrastructure.

Capital intensity overwhelms returns

Alphabet continues deploying extraordinary amounts of capital without a corresponding increase in normalized future free cash flow.

Robotics remains isolated

Gemini Robotics progresses technically but never gains strategic or economic connection to the broader Gemini and Cloud stack.

Regulation blocks the graph

Alphabet's ability to connect identity, context, applications and execution is materially restricted in major markets.

